1
00:00:01,390 --> 00:00:07,810
We are all familiar with one or another form of near field communication enabled devices.

2
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:08,980
What's.

3
00:00:09,010 --> 00:00:11,650
Near field communication and applications.

4
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:18,070
As I said before, near field communication is a technology to transfer information between devices

5
00:00:18,070 --> 00:00:21,010
in proximity using RF signals.

6
00:00:21,730 --> 00:00:29,920
NFC technology offers a wide range of features, from keyless access to smart tags for medical applications,

7
00:00:31,360 --> 00:00:42,070
the option to implement and embed it into credit cards, smartphones and other wearable devices makes

8
00:00:42,070 --> 00:00:45,550
NFC technology one of the most convenient ones.

9
00:00:45,790 --> 00:00:49,450
So let's have a look at the different NFC applications.

10
00:00:51,340 --> 00:01:00,790
First of all, smart cards payment using NFC integrated smart cards offer easier payment compared to

11
00:01:00,790 --> 00:01:03,700
the conventional multiple step payment process.

12
00:01:04,690 --> 00:01:11,050
Top payment services like Visa and Smart Card are offering NFC embedded smart cards to customers.

13
00:01:11,950 --> 00:01:19,030
NFC integrated smart cards can be used for fast payment at grocery shops, parking tickets, adding

14
00:01:19,030 --> 00:01:24,040
shopping points, reading coupons with just a single tap of the card.

15
00:01:24,220 --> 00:01:29,650
All the major banks around the globe offer smart cards with integrated NFC chips.

16
00:01:31,630 --> 00:01:37,180
Second, we have e-wallet, which means payment using a smartphone.

17
00:01:39,030 --> 00:01:46,590
Cashless payment system using mobile devices became popular at the beginning of this decade, and more

18
00:01:46,590 --> 00:01:53,520
services are offering cashless payment for customers convenience using smartphone applications.

19
00:01:53,520 --> 00:01:58,320
Payment can be made using a simple tap or waving the card within proximity.

20
00:01:59,320 --> 00:02:06,850
Service providers can integrate a payment option into smartphones using an NFC tag embedded inside the

21
00:02:06,850 --> 00:02:07,690
device.

22
00:02:07,900 --> 00:02:14,680
Apple pay, Google Wallet, Android Pay, and Samsung Pay are the most popular smartphone payment systems.

23
00:02:15,370 --> 00:02:20,980
Data transfer using the smart device is possible using NFC technology like Android Beam.

24
00:02:21,820 --> 00:02:28,300
Two users can share documents, photos, resumes, and business cards by just waving their smartphones.

25
00:02:29,350 --> 00:02:31,480
Then we have smart ticketing.

26
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:39,280
Integrated smart chips can be used to replace traditional ticketing system with smart tickets for airlines,

27
00:02:39,280 --> 00:02:48,550
train and bus tickets, etc. NFC tags can be used for smart posters, movie tickets, tickets to concerts,

28
00:02:48,550 --> 00:02:51,940
advertisements, flyers, and information links.

29
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:59,920
Customers will be able to access a reserved area or activate tickets by just tapping NFC tags located

30
00:02:59,920 --> 00:03:01,720
at the assigned location.

31
00:03:03,320 --> 00:03:07,550
More information, for example, can be found by just scanning the smart tag.

32
00:03:08,390 --> 00:03:11,480
Then we have medicine and health care for example.

33
00:03:11,630 --> 00:03:16,370
So NFC integrated systems can be used in medicine and health care activities.

34
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:24,770
NFC offers greater accuracy and convenience in prescribing medicine, easier check in payments, checking

35
00:03:24,770 --> 00:03:30,530
the status of patients and tracking records by embedding NFC tags to patient charts.

36
00:03:31,160 --> 00:03:34,940
NFC integrated devices can be easily paired and configured.

37
00:03:35,720 --> 00:03:41,090
Medical professionals can easily check schedules and access medical devices and equipment.

38
00:03:41,780 --> 00:03:47,810
The future of NFC in health care is very promising, and many companies have already started investing.

39
00:03:48,170 --> 00:03:54,890
Diagnostic tests are under development for monitoring medical conditions like temperature variations.

40
00:03:56,340 --> 00:03:59,790
Blood glucose level fluctuation, etc., etc..

41
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:03,590
Fifth, we have keyless access.

42
00:04:03,950 --> 00:04:08,930
Keyless access is one of the familiar applications of near-field communication today.

43
00:04:08,960 --> 00:04:13,580
NFC is convenient and easy to implement feature make it a popular choice.

44
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:20,899
NFC and RFID tags can be used for access to doors and restricted area with a node to detect feature.

45
00:04:21,470 --> 00:04:28,070
It can be used to replace access keys and identification badges, and for easier access to cars and

46
00:04:28,070 --> 00:04:29,090
other vehicles.

47
00:04:33,980 --> 00:04:36,350
Then we have manufacturing.

48
00:04:36,350 --> 00:04:43,820
Smart tags are used in motor manufacturing industries to identify each product from its different processing

49
00:04:43,820 --> 00:04:51,200
stages within the company packaging, transportation, and tracking of products during shipment.

50
00:04:51,500 --> 00:04:58,490
Unique identification numbers allow manufacturers to efficiently manage products in case of return during

51
00:04:58,490 --> 00:05:02,120
the warranty period for replacement, service, and maintenance.

52
00:05:03,270 --> 00:05:05,700
Then we have logistics and shipping.

53
00:05:06,390 --> 00:05:11,910
NFC and RFID tags can be conveniently used in the logistics and shipping industry.

54
00:05:12,210 --> 00:05:18,420
Tracking and scanning of goods using smart tags makes the system smart, errorless, and efficient.

55
00:05:19,740 --> 00:05:22,590
Eighth, we have smart inventory management.

56
00:05:22,830 --> 00:05:29,940
For example, retail shops and large scale supermarkets can make use of smart RFID tags for better management

57
00:05:29,940 --> 00:05:31,980
of inventories in their system.

58
00:05:32,460 --> 00:05:38,910
Smart inventory management software can give a real time update on products details for customers and

59
00:05:38,910 --> 00:05:44,820
items in their inventory stock, and it could trigger automatic orders if a particular item has a low

60
00:05:44,820 --> 00:05:45,510
quantity.

61
00:05:46,730 --> 00:05:51,470
Vendors will get an update on items in high demand and better service can be provided.

62
00:05:52,430 --> 00:05:54,560
Ninth, we have the theft control.

63
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:59,120
Another attractive use of RFID tags is theft control.

64
00:05:59,150 --> 00:06:03,260
Valuable things can be protected using smart tags.

65
00:06:03,290 --> 00:06:07,520
Objects embedded with smart tags will trigger if they pass by RFID.

66
00:06:07,520 --> 00:06:08,330
Proximity.

67
00:06:09,200 --> 00:06:12,860
The active area where the RFID transmitter is installed.

68
00:06:13,760 --> 00:06:22,070
Finally, we have NFC information tags similar to QR code scanning using a smartphone camera.

69
00:06:22,370 --> 00:06:25,730
Users can access information with NFC tags.

70
00:06:26,150 --> 00:06:32,870
If someone wants to access information about product or service, for example, it can be accessed by

71
00:06:32,870 --> 00:06:35,690
just tapping their phone on the NFC Smart Tag.

